      "transcriber_notes": [
        "No column headings are printed; the table is a bracketed classification. Column names in [brackets] are supplied by the transcriber: [Group] = the name printed at left and joined by a brace; [Division] = the intermediate name (only 'Khalka'); [People / Tribe] = each entry line; [Habitat] = the region printed at right.",
        "Where a brace joins several entries to one habitat (or group), that habitat/group is repeated on each row it covers.",
        "Part I: the 'Sharra or Eastern Mongolians' left brace covers Khalka (Tushetu, Tsi-tseng, Jasaktu, (Sain-noin)) and the paired entries Uchumsin : Chakar ... Ordos; paired names printed 'X : Y' on one line are kept as one entry. The right brace 'S., E. and S.E. Mongolia' is read as covering Uchumsin ... Naiman, with Ordos against 'N. bend of the Huang-ho'.",
        "Part I: Urianghai, Sok-pa and Taldi (?) are printed at the group-name indent with no brace; given with [Group] empty. In the Tungus Family, 'Manchuria' is braced to Manchus/Tungus and 'Upper Ili Valley, Kuldja' to Solons/Sibos. In the Turki Family, 'Kuldja' is braced to Taranchi and Kirghiz-Kazaks; the left brace is read as including Taranchi.",
        "Part II: the Si-fan entries are printed at the top of p. 86 (p0105), before heading III, and belong to part II. 'Bod-pa Tibetans proper)' printed with a closing parenthesis only — as printed. 'Kansi, Kokonor, Tsaidam' printed 'Kansi' (possibly a misprint for Kansu) — as printed.",
        "Part III: 'extinct ?' is printed with a brace against Chimpan and Khato-zun; appended to each of those entries in parentheses. 'Kuldja' is braced to Khambing, Chimpan and Khato-zun.",
        "Part IV: 'Miaotze or Nanman Group' brace covers Pe-Lolo through Tung. The right brace beside Pe-Lolo/Shu-Lolo/He-Lolo carries two lines, 'S. bend of the Yangtze' (level with Shu-Lolo) and 'S. Szechuan, N. Yunnan' (level with He-Lolo); how they divide among the three is not clear, so both are given, separated by ' / ', on each row. 'Kilao. Kitao' printed with a full stop — as printed.",
        "Line-break hyphen removed in 'Tanguts (Northern Tibetans)' (printed 'Ti-' / 'betans'). 'Tu-man' is printed 'Tu-' / 'man' across a line break; kept hyphenated, as it cannot be told whether the hyphen is part of the name.",
        "All question marks ('Taldi (?)', '? About source of Yangtze', '? Central Lake region, Tibet', 'extinct ?', 'Kara-Kultsi (?)') are printed in the source; they are not transcriber uncertainty.",
        "No totals printed.",
        "74 data rows counted on the pages (I: 30, II: 10, III: 9, IV: 22, V: 3); 74 transcribed."
      ],
